description: Prettier type imports named types and catalog versions
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code style

Match the nearest file. Let Prettier format it. It uses single quotes, no semicolons, 2-space indent, trailing commas `es5`, print width 80. Do not add `;` after statements Prettier will strip them.

Import types with `import type` or an inline `type` specifier. Group imports as React, then third-party packages, then `@repo/*`, then relative, with a blank line between groups.

Prefer `export type Name = { ... }` over `interface`. Prefer `export function Name` over a default export. Prefix unused arguments with `_`.

Names we own are camelCase (`toolCalls`, not `tool_calls`). Leave snake_case on a library object and read it in one helper. Do not copy that shape onto our types.

Put shared library versions in the workspace `catalog` and depend on them with `"catalog:"`. Depend on other packages in this repo with `"workspace:*"`.

Do not restate the comments, CSS-module, schema vs db, or split-by-job rules.

```ts
// BAD
import { AgentToolCall } from '@repo/agent-client'
interface Props {
  tools: AgentToolCall[]
}
export default function Board(props: Props) {}

// GOOD
import type { AgentToolCall } from '@repo/agent-client'

export type ChatBoardProps = {
  tools: AgentToolCall[]
}

export function ChatBoard({ tools }: ChatBoardProps) {}
```
